{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "30", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "07", "M": "50", "S": "59"}}, "news": [{"title": "Mangaluru development body eases land approvals, cuts regularisation fee to 1%", "para": "Mangaluru's property owners rejoice! New government measures have significantly reduced regularisation fees for unauthorised land subdivisions and simplified the approval process for both old and new subdivisions. The necessity for separate land conversion orders in Muda\u2019s master plan has been lifted. To enhance clarity, a public helpdesk is being established at the Muda office, designed to facilitate a smoother approval experience for property owners.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/mangaluru-development-body-eases-land-approvals-cuts-regularisation-fee-to-1/135347362?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-289648/135347362.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Mumbai: Dharavi building residents to get 500-sq-ft rehabilitation flats", "para": "Residents of Dharavi are on the brink of transformation through the Dharavi Redevelopment Project. A recent announcement from the state urban development department details the criteria for receiving rehab flats. Each qualifying resident will be allocated a 300 sq-foot space at no charge, with an extra 35% fungible area accessible for some. This strategic project focuses on tackling housing challenges and elevating living conditions in the bustling locality.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/mumbai-dharavi-building-residents-to-get-500-sq-ft-rehabilitation-flats/135343239?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-321768/135343239.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Consumer court orrders Ghaziabad's Krishna Infocom  to refund buyer's money over delay", "para": "The consumer disputes commission has mandated Krishna Infocom to refund Rs 3.7 lakh to Sushma Gupta, who had booked a flat in 2013 but never received possession by the promised January 2020 date. Despite her efforts for resolution, Gupta only received a partial refund of Rs 1 lakh. The ruling against Shyam Builders highlights prevalent issues in property transactions and consumer rights protection within India.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/consumer-court-orrders-ghaziabads-krishna-infocom-to-refund-buyers-money-over-delay/135342746?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-83866/135342746.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}